Step 2 – Decide which fields need protection:
• We compare the current threat level of each field. Many fields on the farm have very low threat levels (for instance Field_1 (0.01), Field_2 (0.00), Field_3 (0.02), Field_4 (0.00), Field_5 (0.03), Field_6 (0.00), Field_7 (0.05), Field_8 (0.02) and Field_9 (0.05)). In contrast, the highest‐threat fields – for example Field_10 (0.11), Field_11 (0.13), Field_12 (0.13), Field_14 (0.10), Field_15 (0.10), Field_16 (0.28), Field_18 (0.16), Field_21 (0.22), Field_25 (0.14), Field_26 (0.20), Field_27 (0.15), Field_30 (0.11), Field_34 (0.15), Field_36 (0.14), Field_37 (0.10), Field_39 (0.11), Field_40 (0.16), Field_44 (0.13), Field_46 (0.17), Field_47 (0.10), Field_51 (0.20), Field_52 (0.12), Field_54 (0.13), Field_56 (0.19), Field_58 (0.25), Field_59 (0.12), Field_62 (0.12), Field_65 (0.14), Field_66 (0.22), Field_70 (0.17), Field_73 (0.17), Field_81 (0.14), Field_82 (0.14), Field_84 (0.17), Field_86 (0.33), Field_88 (0.13), Field_94 (0.18), Field_96 (0.23), Field_104 (0.11), Field_105 (0.13), Field_112 (0.22), Field_117 (0.11), Field_119 (0.22), Field_121 (0.23), Field_127 (0.18), Field_131 (0.12), Field_134 (0.10) and Field_138 (0.20) – are the ones that need protection.
 
Step 3 – For each field that needs protection, keep any drones already protecting the field in position.
 
Step 4 – For fields that need protection but that currently have no drones protecting them, assign additional drones based on proximity to the field. In our situation the available drone fleet is largely committed to flying toward fields that have very low threat levels. As a result it is best to reassign drones from low‐threat fields and from the “moving” pool so that only the highest–threat fields are actually assigned protection.
 
Step 5 – Final assignment decision:
Because no drones are originally targeting any of the high–threat fields (Field_10, Field_11, Field_12, Field_14, Field_15, Field_16, Field_18, Field_21, Field_25, Field_26, Field_27, Field_30, Field_34, Field_36, Field_37, Field_39, Field_40, Field_44, Field_46, Field_47, Field_51, Field_52, Field_54, Field_56, Field_58, Field_59, Field_62, Field_65, Field_66, Field_70, Field_73, Field_81, Field_82, Field_84, Field_86, Field_88, Field_94, Field_96, Field_104, Field_105, Field_112, Field_117, Field_119, Field_121, Field_127, Field_131, Field_134, Field_138) – and since drones already “protecting” or moving to fields (like Field_1, Field_2, Field_4, Field_6, Field_7, Field_8, Field_9 or Field_140) are assigned to fields that, from a threat‐priority viewpoint, do not require protection, the sensible coordinator decision is to reassign almost every drone away from protection and have the majority go idle.
