• Field_9 (threat 0.03, quota=6): Five drones are already protecting it (Drone_63, Drone_115, Drone_116, Drone_169 and Drone_207). Therefore, Field_9 needs one more drone.
(Other fields with assigned drone‐targets – such as Field_1, Field_4, Field_6, Field_8 and Field_140 – have threat levels of 0.00 so they do not “need” additional protection.)

Step 2 – Decide which fields need additional protection:
Based on threat levels and full‐protection quotas the only fields that call for additional active protection are Field_2 (needs 2 more) and Field_3 (needs 3) and Field_9 (needs 1 more). (Even though Field_5 and Field_7 already have protecting drones they are not “red‐flagged” for extra help and the remaining fields have threat 0.00 so do not need active protection.) 

Step 3 – Retain already protecting drones on fields that need protection:
• For Field_2, keep Drone_209 and Drone_210 in “protecting Field_2.”
• For Field_3, no drone is yet protecting it.
• For Field_5, keep Drone_14 and Drone_216 as “protecting Field_5.”
