All other drones – including those whose target fields are already well protected or which are aimed at fields whose threat level is zero – will be assigned as “idle.”

Step 5 – Final group assignments:
For each drone we now assign its group. Drones already protecting a needed field remain in their “protecting” group; the chosen additional drones for Field_2, Field_3 and Field_9 are assigned to the corresponding protecting group; all the rest become “idle.” Note that among the allowed groups only “protecting Field_2”, “protecting Field_3”, “protecting Field_5”, “protecting Field_7” and “protecting Field_9” will be used. (Even if a drone is “protecting” a field such as Field_1, Field_4, Field_6, Field_8 or Field_140, these fields are not among the allowed groups so those drones are reassigned to “idle.”)

