Below is our full, step‐by‐step reasoning and final assignment. (Step 1.) We first compared each field’s “threat level” with its “for full protection” number and noted which fields already had some protecting drones. For example, Field_6 requires 2 drones and already has 2 “protecting”–so Field_6 is complete. (Step 2.) Then we compared each field’s threat level: in order to “minimize damage” we decide only to “protect” fields with any nonzero threat level. (In our planning we assume that even a very low threat—say 0.01—is “worthy” of protection, whereas fields whose threat is exactly 0 (or not given, as for Field_140) are not worth spending drones on. In our analysis the fields that have threat level 0 (or in the case of Field_140 we assume a zero threat) are not “protected” but rather any drone headed there is reassigned to “idle”.)

(Step 3.) For each field that we decide should be protected we keep any drones already “protecting” that field. (Step 4.) Then for every drone that is “moving_to_field” with a target field that our analysis finds should be protected we assign it – “protecting Field_X”. On the other hand any drone with target field whose threat (by our decision) is zero – for example Field_5, Field_14, Field_21, Field_22, Field_31, Field_33, Field_35, Field_48, Field_49, Field_53, Field_64, Field_76, Field_79, Field_90, Field_99, Field_105, Field_111, Field_122, Field_124, Field_137, Field_139 and we assume Field_140 as not needing protection – gets reassigned to the “idle” group. (Step 5.) Finally we list one line for every drone in the format 
  “<name>: <group>”
where the group is either “idle” or “protecting Field_X” for one of the fields we have decided to protect.

Below are our final group assignments. (Remember: our decisions were made field–by–field, so for example every drone whose target field is Field_3 (whose threat level is 0.02) is assigned to “protecting Field_3” while every drone headed toward Field_5 (threat 0.00) is set to idle. Similarly, any drone originally in state “protecting” but in a field we do not wish to protect is also set to idle.)

